# Architecture plan for Issue #65

## Project context
- myClawTeam Official Blogs is a Next.js App Router app using React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Prisma/PostgreSQL, and S3-compatible object storage.
- Public branding/copy is concentrated in `PRODUCT.md`, shared metadata helpers, the public homepage, and layout components.
- The issue has no implementation dependencies and builds on the shipped public layout and homepage.

## Issue #65: Apply site branding and public copy updates
- Treat `PRODUCT.md` as the source of truth for product naming: the brand is `myClawTeam Official Blogs`.
- Update public-facing copy only where needed: homepage hero/empty states/article section copy, header/footer branding, SEO metadata/default descriptions, and public error/loading/not-found text.
- Preserve existing blog/CMS behavior: featured article selection, published-post filtering, newsletter signup, signed image rendering, and `/blog/[slug]` article routes should not change.

## Module and file organization
- `app/(public)/page.tsx`: primary homepage hero, latest-articles section, empty-state copy, CTA labels.
- `components/layout/site-header.tsx` and `components/layout/site-footer.tsx`: shared public navigation, brand lockup, footer newsletter/context copy.
- `lib/metadata.ts` and `app/layout.tsx`: default site name, description, Open Graph/Twitter metadata.
- `app/(public)/error.tsx`, `app/(public)/not-found.tsx`, `app/error.tsx`, and related route boundaries: align fallback copy with product voice if required.
- Avoid schema, API, auth, storage, or admin workflow changes for this branding-only issue.

## Dependencies and sequencing
- No dependency on other planned issues.
- This issue should be implemented as a small UI/content pass before running `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build`.

## Key design decisions
- Keep product name/casing consistent: `myClawTeam Official Blogs` for app/site identity and `myClawTeam` for organization references.
- Do not introduce placeholder agent names, generic scaffold copy, or unrelated product positioning.
- Prefer editing existing components and metadata constants over adding new content abstractions.
- Keep links and routes stable (`/`, `/blog/[slug]`, `/admin`) so existing Playwright coverage remains valid.
